    "Show that $G$ is isomorphic to some semi-direct product of $P$\nby $Q$. (There is a theorem that says if certain hypotheses hold for\n$P$ and $Q$ then $G$ is isomorphic to a semi-direct product of $P$ by\n$Q$. State that theorem and prove that those hypotheses on $P$ and $Q$\nhold here. You do not have to prove the theorem itself.)"}
