 {:number 1,
  :subparts
  [{:label "(a)",
    :body
    "Show that $A$ is generated (as a group) by some subset of a basis\nof $V$."}
   {:label "(b)",
    :body
    "Suppose $G\\subset GL(V)$ is a finite subgroup of the group of\ninvertible linear endomorphisms of $V$ over $\\Q$. Suppose $B\\subset V$\nis a finitely generated abelian group. Let $B'$ be the subgroup\ngenerated by all $g(B)$ for all $g\\in G$. You may assume these (easy)\nfacts: $B'$ is finitely generated; $B\\subset B'\\subset V$ and\n$g(B')\\subset B'$ for all $g\\in G$. \n\nLet $\\Z$ be the ring of integers and let $R$ be a commutative\nring. The group of $n\\times n$ matrices over $R$ with inverses that\nare also matrices over $R$ is denoted $GL_n(R)$.\n\nSuppose $GL_n(\\Q)$ is the group of invertible $n\\times n$ matrices and\n$G\\subset GL_n(\\Q)$ is a finite subgroup. Show that there is a $P\\in\nGL_n(\\Q)$ such that $PGP^{-1}=\\{PgP^{-1}\\pipe g\\in G\\}\\subset\nGL_n(\\Z)$."}
   {:label "(c)",
    :body
    "If $f:R\\rightarrow S$ is a ring homomorphism, there is a natural\ngroup homomorphism $GL_n(f):GL_n(R)\\rightarrow GL_n(S)$ defined by\nletting $f$ act on each entry. \n\nLet $m\\geq 2$. Show that the kernel of the natural map\n$GL_n(\\Z/p^m\\Z)\\rightarrow GL_n(\\Z/p^{m-1}\\Z)$ is abelian. Hint: this\nkernel consists of elements of the form $1+p^{m-1}A$ for $A\\in\nM_n(\\Z/p^m\\Z)$, the ring of matrices over $\\Z/p^m\\Z$."}
   {:label "(d)",
    :body
    "Suppose that $G\\subset GL_n(\\Q)$ as above is a finite simple group.\nShow that there is an injection $G\\rightarrow GL_n(\\Z/p\\Z)$ for any\nprime $p$."}],
