 {:number 2,
  :subparts
  [{:label "(a)",
    :body
    "Let $F\\subset E$ be a Galois extension of fields. Show that\nthere is a field $A$ with $F\\subset A\\subset E$ such that\n%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\n%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\n\\begin{rlist}"}
   {:label "(b)", :body "$A/F$ is Galois and"}
   {:label "(c)", :body "the Galois group of $A/F$ is abelian and"}
   {:label "(d)",
    :body
    "if $K$ is any field with $F\\subset K\\subset E$ with $K/F$ Galois\nand with the Galois group $K/F$ abelian, then $K\\subset A$. (Thus, $A$\nis the unique largest field between $F$ and $E$ satisfying (i) and\n(ii).)\n\\end{rlist}\n%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\n%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%"}
   {:label "(e)",
    :body
    "With $F\\subset A\\subset E$ as in part (a), suppose that $K$ is a\nfield with $F\\subset K\\subset E$. Show that the following things are\nequivalent\n%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\n%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\n\\begin{rlist}"}
   {:label "(f)",
    :body "$K/F$ is Galois and the Galois group of $K/F$ is abelian."}
   {:label "(g)",
    :body
    "$K\\subset A$.\n\\end{rlist}\n%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\n%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%"}
   {:label "(h)",
    :body
    "Let $F$ be a field having algebraic closure $\\Omega$. Let\n$F\\subset E\\subset \\Omega$ and $F\\subset L\\subset \\Omega$. Suppose\nthat $E$ and $L$ are Galois extensions of $F$. Show that $E\\cap L$ is\na Galois extension of $F$."}
   {:label "(i)",
    :body
    "Let $F,L,E$ and $\\Omega$ be as in part (c). (In particular, we\nassume that $E/F$ and $L/F$ are Galois.) Considering the Galois\nextension $F\\subset E$, let $A(E)$ be the field $A$ discussed in part\n(a). Analogously, define $A(L)$ and $A(E\\cap L)$. (So, for instance,\n$A(E\\cap L)$ is the largest field between $F$ and $E\\cap L$ such that\n$A(E\\cap L)/F$ is Galois and has an abelian Galois group.)\n\nShow that $A(E\\cap L)=A(E)\\cap A(L)$."}],
